preConditionHook:
// EL: avgTailFraction = Average((high - low - AbsValue(close - open))
//         / (high - low + epsilon), tailBars).
//
// The averaged quantity is the NON-BODY fraction of the bar -- both tails
// together -- so the statistic carries no direction and both sides read the
// same value. That is the distinction from AverageUpperTailFraction, which
// averages ONE tail and mirrors the sides: a bar with a huge lower tail and a
// shaved top passes that rule's long side and fails this one.
//
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808)
// and the averaged quantity is a price EXPRESSION with real history, not an EL
// variable -- so this is a fresh loop over price, NOT the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange
// rolling accumulator and NOT the zero-filled variable mirror BarRangeAboveStd
// needs. Summed newest-first, EasyLanguage's Summation order.
//
// The epsilon is the corpus's zero-range guard (CloseRangePosition's literal,
// carried as an input so the ratio's low bits match the twin): EasyLanguage
// raises a RUNTIME divide-by-zero error on a zero denominator, so it is added
// inside the ratio rather than branched around.
//
// The accumulator is a class member and persists across bars, so it is reset
// before the loop.
avgTailFraction = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)tailBars; ++i) {
    avgTailFraction += (high[i] - low[i] - std::fabs(close[i] - open[i])) / (high[i] - low[i] + epsilon);
}
avgTailFraction /= (int)tailBars;
